        <mxCell id="tl-note-body" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;rounded=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;fontSize=12;fontColor=#555;" value="•  &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:monospace;&quot;&gt;NUM_TIMESTEPS&lt;/span&gt; (30) — the inner loop runs this many times; everything inside it scales linearly.&lt;br&gt;•  Linear layers use parallel MAC: &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:monospace;&quot;&gt;linear_layer&lt;/span&gt; latency = 1 + ⌈NUM_OUTPUTS / PARALLELISM⌉ · (NUM_INPUTS + 1) cycles; one done pulse.&lt;br&gt;     fc1 (4 → 64, P = 16): 1 + 4·5 = 21 cycles, runs once.   fc2 (64 → 16, P = 16): 1 + 1·65 = 66 cycles, runs each timestep.&lt;br&gt;•  Neuron processing per timestep (HL1 LIFs run concurrently with fc2 and are typically hidden under fc2 latency):&lt;br&gt;     baseline LIF = 1 cycle (HL1 + HL2 both negligible vs fc2).&lt;br&gt;     fractional LIF: HL2 adds a TS_HL2_WAIT drain of ≈ &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:monospace;&quot;&gt;HISTORY_LENGTH + 5&lt;/span&gt; cycles per timestep.&lt;br&gt;     bitshift   LIF: HL2 adds a TS_HL2_WAIT drain of ≈ &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:monospace;&quot;&gt;HISTORY_LENGTH + 6&lt;/span&gt; cycles per timestep (one extra ST_POST register stage).&lt;br&gt;•  Per-timestep total: baseline ≈ fc2 + 5;   fractional ≈ fc2 + &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:monospace;&quot;&gt;H + 10&lt;/span&gt;;   bitshift ≈ fc2 + &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:monospace;&quot;&gt;H + 11&lt;/span&gt;.&lt;br&gt;     baseline default: 66 + 5 = 71 cycles/t  →  30 timesteps = 2130 cycles.&lt;br&gt;•  q_accumulator finalization: NUM_TIMESTEPS · (NUM_NEURONS / &lt;span style=&quot;font-family:monospace;&quot;&gt;Q_BATCH_SIZE&lt;/span&gt; + 4) + 2 cycles  →  30 · (16/4 + 4) + 2 = 242 cycles with defaults.&lt;br&gt;•  Approximate total (baseline LIF, defaults): 21 (fc1) + 2130 (loop) + 242 (q_acc) ≈ &lt;b&gt;2400 cycles&lt;/b&gt;  →  ~24 µs at 100 MHz.&lt;br&gt;&lt;i&gt;Latency is set by these architectural parameters; it does not depend on the input observation values.&lt;/i&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="940" x="45" y="512" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
